
.SH TABLE OF CONTENTS
.nf  
A) overview        general overview of comments/docs
B) technical       how it is handled
C) koios           system generated
D) saved           temporary save or comment out
E) breaks          line spacers

.SH A) OVERVIEW
non-execution lines are added to space, structure, and inform; but do not
alter execution in any way.

.SH B) TECHNICAL
none of these documentation or comment lines are carried over to code.

.SH C) KOIOS
koios provided comments all start with a hash (#)...

   ---file-header-----------------------------------------------------------
   #!/usr/local/bin/koios
   #   koios-polos (axis of heaven) unit testing meta-language

   ---between-scripts-------------------------------------------------------
   #23456789-12 § 123456789-123456789-123456789-12345 § ´´´
   #==(verb)=== § ===========(description)=========== § ´´´

   ---file-footer-----------------------------------------------------------
   # end-of-file.  done, finito, completare, whimper [Ï´···

.SH D) SAVED
to save lines through updates and conversions without them making it into
the unit-text executable, start with (#>)...

   ---general-note----------------------------------------------------------
   #>  wave 0    01    is not dependent outside files/functions

   ---temporarily-commented-out---------------------------------------------
   #> local     § create working variable             § ´´´

   ---temporarily-saving-a-macro--------------------------------------------
   #> macro  @b  lllllllR-··¥··lllll.lllll.llllll

.SH E) BREAKS
in many data validation blocks, a huge number of steps build up without
anything to visually give it structure.  a line break dose that for me.

the verb is "Ï>----´".  the rest is system generated.  the verb must be
indented by five (5) spaces.

